## 5. Edge Computing in Real-Time Personalization

Real‐time personalization demands low latency and privacy‐preserving computation, driving the adoption of edge computing. By offloading critical inference tasks to on‐device AI accelerators, applications can deliver instantaneous UI adaptations without round trips to the cloud.

Edge AI frameworks now support on‐device deep learning for UI personalization, enabling private models to learn from local user data in real time and apply personalized adjustments—dark mode toggles, font scaling, or content ordering—without transmitting sensitive information offline. This decentralization reduces bandwidth usage, ensures compliance with stringent data regulations, and improves responsiveness in low‐connectivity environments.

Frameworks such as TensorFlow Lite and Core ML have evolved to support incremental model updates via federated learning on edge devices, enhancing the personalization model’s performance while respecting user privacy. Early adopter case studies from healthcare and automotive sectors report a 20% reduction in model inference latency and a 30% improvement in personalization accuracy due to edge‐driven enhancements.

