## 8. Federated Learning for Privacy-Preserving Personalization

As privacy concerns escalate, federated learning (FL) offers a pathway to train personalization models on decentralized user data without central data collection. Parties download a base model, refine it on local devices using private data, and send only parameter updates—never raw personal information—for secure aggregation.

Recent research has explored federated meta‐learning techniques to accelerate personalization with minimal data, employing local fine‐tuning steps that adapt global model parameters to individual usage patterns. These approaches reduce the risk of data leakage, comply with data-protection regulations, and maintain high personalization performance. Real‐world pilots in healthcare and finance sectors report up to 40% reduction in personalization drift, with all user data remaining on‐device throughout the process.

