## 12. AI Co-Designers and Generative UI Prototyping Tools

AI‐powered design tools have matured to become co‐designers, from early ideation to fully interactive prototypes. Solutions like Uizard’s Autodesigner allow designers to generate multi‐screen prototypes from simple text prompts and refine them iteratively. Designers can describe use cases (“create a mobile checkout flow with minimal steps”) and receive editable UI drafts within seconds.

These generative tools accelerate design cycles and democratize UI prototyping, enabling non-technical stakeholders to contribute to interface iterations. As these systems grow in sophistication, AI co-designers become integral to the personalization workflow, quickly generating variations tailored to user segments and A/B testing them in real time.

